# Topic 3 — Data Entry and Headers

## Objective

Practice entering and organizing structured data in Excel using a practical Pinterest Analytics dataset.

## Skills Practiced

- Entered data into Excel cells
- Edited existing cell values
- Deleted and re-entered data
- Used Enter and Tab for data entry
- Created meaningful column headers
- Organized data into rows and columns
- Practiced structured dataset creation
- Applied basic header formatting
- Created a Pinterest Analytics dataset

## Dataset Structure

The dataset contains Pinterest performance data with the following columns:

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| Date | Date the Pin was published |
| Pin_Title | Title of the Pinterest Pin |
| Category | Product/content category |
| Impressions | Number of times the Pin was shown |
| Engagements | Number of interactions |
| Saves | Number of times the Pin was saved |
| Outbound_Clicks | Number of clicks leading outside Pinterest |

## Dataset

The practice dataset contains 15 Pinterest Pin records.

Example categories include:

- Lunch Box
- Storage
- Kitchen Organization
- Beauty
- Home Gadget
- Handbag

## Key Learning

A well-structured dataset should have:

- One variable per column
- One record per row
- Clear and meaningful column headers
- Consistent data entry

## Practical Application

This dataset will be used in later Excel topics for:

- Calculations
- Functions
- Sorting and filtering
- Conditional formatting
- Data analysis
- Dashboard creation

